target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckReadsOmittedBranchesFromGit'
expect: was not read from git
why:    -branch defaults to "" and nothing filled it, so an omitted flag refused every push with "current or default branch unknown" on an ordinary feature branch — recorded twice in the friction log (2026-10-16, 2026-10-20). The branch is a git fact, which push-check.py's own docstring filed it as; reading it from git in -repo is the fallback, and only what git cannot name stays unknown.
--- old
	if branch == "" {
		branch = currentBranch(p.Repo)
	}
--- new
